a heartfelt speech a somber agreement a  prank involving zombies it's moments  like these that make the big bang theory  legendary even years after its final rap  these are the show's biggest moments  ranked from good to best  in the early seasons of the big bang  theory it's easy to wonder why leonard  lives with sheldon in the first place  given how difficult he can be leonard  answers this question in season three's  the staircase implementation when he  tells penny the story of how he became  sheldon's roommate when leonard started  his job as a researcher at caltech he  needed to rent an apartment nearby he  met sheldon when the latter was  subletting his apartment as his previous  roommate sebastian could no longer stand  to live with him at that time sheldon  made leonard answer a bunch of  ridiculous questions before reluctantly  allowing him to move in the two didn't  get along at first and leonard avoided  having to hang out with sheldon  preferring instead to conduct home  experiments with howard played by simon  helberg and raj played by kunal nayar  but one such experiment quickly turned  dangerous when the rocket fuel leonard  had created started malfunctioning it  was sheldon's quick thinking that  prevented the fuel from exploding in  their apartment leonard felt indebted to  sheldon and the two quickly became good  friends thereafter you're welcome  the most important way in which sheldon  retains power and his friendship with  leonard is through the elaborate  roommate agreement signed by leonard  when he first moved in the agreement  contains elaborate rules for the code of  conduct between him and sheldon as  roommates and friends naturally the  agreement is heavily skewed in sheldon's  favor but leonard's one-time girlfriend  priya played by arnie mann isn't so  easily controlled by the paradigms of  the agreement free is a lawyer and  doesn't appreciate the way sheldon  rigged the agreement to give himself  power over leonard in the agreement  dissection in season 4 priya argues  around the clauses in the contract much  to leonard's delay sheldon then  threatens to expose priya's relationship  with leonard to her disapproving parents  if the original terms of the agreement  aren't reinstated at priya's urging  leonard concedes to sheldon's demands  leaving him once again the ruler of  their little apartment kingdom  sheldon never shows much interest in  following the dictates of conventional  society his genius intellect and  anti-social nature often combine to  create a perfect storm of insufferable  behavior and it usually falls on leonard  to keep sheldon in line during his most  eccentric moments one of the biggest  instances of this occurs in season 3  with the einstein approximation in which  sheldon has been stuck on a problem at  work regarding the behavior of electrons  this leads him to try increasingly  bizarre ways to wrap his brain around  the issue while foregoing the usual  pesky human weaknesses of food and sleep  it's left to leonard to try to keep a  handle on the sleep-deprived lunatic his  roommate becomes sheldon works all night  on a whiteboard trying unsuccessfully to  solve his problem which he promptly  tosses into the street the next morning  causing a car crash sheldon also lays  out intricate patterns of marbles in the  living room in a bid to understand the  movement of electrons which causes penny  and leonard to slip and fall painfully  his crowning moment however is when  leonard is forced to follow sheldon into  a kid's ball pit that the latter swims  around in like scrooge mcduck shouting  bazinga repeatedly though leonard is  devoted to taking care of sheldon like  an older brother would this often  becomes a sore spot for leonard's  friends who think he's being taken  advantage of leonard has a major  reckoning in the season 5 episode the  friendship contraction you know what i  am sick of the roommate agreement  after a long day of sheldon being his  usual demanding self leonard invokes  clause 209 of the roommate agreement  nullifying the friendship aspect of  their relationship and reducing them to  mere roommates at first sheldon tries to  replace leonard with his other friends  but it quickly becomes apparent that no  one has the patience to deal with him  desperate to have leonard back but  loathe to admit defeat sheldon resorts  to turning off the entire building's  lights in an effort to make leonard need  his help but the ruse doesn't work  finally leonard agrees to reinstate the  friendship clause in return for an  annual leonard's day we set aside a day  to celebrate all your contributions to  my life both actual and imagined by you  one of the most accurate descriptions of  sheldon cooper is provided by leonard  when he tells penny the guy's one lab  accident away from being a super villain  sheldon's machiavellian tendencies are  on full display in the itchy brain  simulation in season seven when leonard  reveals that a forgotten dv david once  rented is seven years overdue he makes a  deal with leonard whereby he must wear  an extremely itchy sweater under his  clothes until he manages to return the  dvd so he can appreciate how  uncomfortable sheldon feels mentally  whenever he's forced to deal with  unfinished business leonard agrees to  the deal and the rest of the episode  sees him growing increasingly desperate  as he continues to wear the sweater  while trying to find a way to return the  dvd in the end it's revealed that  sheldon had paid for the dvd years ago  and was using the situation to teach  leonard a lesson about responsibility  the angry red welts and leonard's body  caused by the sweater at the end of the  episode show just how painful that  lesson is  sheldon's primary character trait  throughout most of the big bang theory  is his overwhelming narcissism he's the  most important person in his life and he  expects his friends to place him in a  similarly important position in their  lives as he amply demonstrates in season  3 with the large hadron collision when  leonard gets the opportunity to go to  switzerland to observe the large hadron  collider he's thrilled to be able to  take his girlfriend penny with him to  celebrate valentine's day when sheldon  hears about leonard's trip however he  assumes his roommate would take him  instead of penny when he discovers  that's not the case he's outraged  throughout the episode sheldon begs  pleads and schemes his way around  convincing leonard to take him  if there's one character in the big bang  theory who seems incapable of changing  it's sheldon cooper who's perennially  convinced that any problem is with  everyone else not him incredibly however  sheldon does begin to change after  meeting amy farah fowler played by mayan  bialik although he's completely  uninterested in romance at first sheldon  begins to date amy as a sort of  experiment he repeatedly insists they  aren't romantically involved but over  time sheldon begins to realize he cares  a great deal more for amy than he was  initially prepared to admit one of the  earliest and most hilarious examples of  this occurs in season 5's the pulled  groin extrapolation at first sheldon  seems completely indifferent to the fact  that leonard and amy had gone to a party  together until he misconstrued something  leonard says as a hint that they've  gotten frisky and karate chops him why'd  you do that to send a message she is not  for you  the joy of sheldon's characterization is  in watching someone with genius  intellect inhabit the body of a  hyperactive man child he has no sense of  social niceties and leonard always acts  as his reluctant caretaker all those  factors combined for a perfect storm of  hilarity in the bozeman reaction in  season three after a night out leonard  and sheldon arrive back at their  apartment to discover that the lock has  been broken and their belongings have  been ransacked although the robbers  didn't take anything of material value  sheldon becomes paranoid at the thought  of another possible break-in throughout  the episode he comes up with  increasingly elaborate anti-burglary  alarms that end up backfiring  hilariously finally sheldon is forced to  conclude that he can no longer live in a  city that's a cesspool of crime and  decides to relocate to a place where  there will be less chance of getting  murdered is he quitting his job at the  university oh no he's going to  telecommute  everybody's really excited about it  throughout the ordeal leonard repeatedly  tries to reassure sheldon that he's safe  in their apartment putting up with all  of his hysterics and ridiculous schemes  we often see leonard taking care of  sheldon and making concessions for his  off-putting behavior to the extent that  leonard almost comes across as a doormat  it's much rarer to see sheldon taking  care of leonard but the truth is despite  taking his friendship for granted most  of the time sheldon does genuinely care  for leonard the sweetest example of his  affection occurs in season six is the  decoupling fluctuation while leonard and  penny are dating it's revealed that  penny has secret doubts about their  relationship when sheldon learns of this  he becomes increasingly agitated with  the weight of the secret and its  potential impact on his friend this  tension causes sheldon to wake penny up  in the middle of the night to tell her  all the ways leonard is a great guy and  prime boyfriend material as the  thoroughly exasperated penny orders  sheldon to leave he finally drops his  usual arrogance and aloofness and  instead has a marked humility that he  reserves for only the most special of  occasions please don't hurt my friend  after many years as sheldon's roommate  leonard had gathered a vast collection  of knowledge about his friend some of  that knowledge is actively uncomfortable  like knowing sheldon's bathroom schedule  but sometimes leonard's expert knowledge  of sheldon's personal life proves  invaluable take the case of the panty  pinata polarization in season two after  a long day of having to deal with  sheldon's nonsense penny finally puts  her foot down and declares she will no  longer follow his rules this results in  penny being banished until she's willing  to apologize and take a class to improve  her attitude when penny proves  unrepentant and hostile it kickstarts an  escalating series of pranks between her  and sheldon that soon threatens to spill  over into violence that's when leonard  tells penny that he knows sheldon's  kryptonite he gives her the phone number  of sheldon's mother mary who swiftly  puts an end to the war and forces  sheldon to apologize  leonard and sheldon can often come  across as immature and ill-equipped to  handle adult life but the fact remains  that both are also top researchers in  their fields whose professional  reputations are quite distinguished  these two factors collide in an epic  manner in the cooper hofstadter  polarization in season 1. leonard and  sheldon write a research paper together  and are subsequently invited to present  it at a conference in front of their  peers sheldon doesn't want to go because  he doesn't think the crowd at the  conference has the necessary genius to  properly appreciate his work an  indignant leonard declares he'll be  going to the conference with or without  his co-author sheldon refuses to allow  leonard to present the paper alone and  also refuses to accompany him a long  petty fight ensues culminating in them  airing out their dirty laundry in front  of the audience at the conference  sheldon attempts to blow leonard's brain  apart using his mind which obviously  doesn't work the whole ordeal later gets  put up on the internet as a lasting  testament to leonard and sheldon's  bizarre relationship  one of sheldon's many quirks is his  hypochondria which is aggravated by his  genius intellect he often envisions  worst case scenarios whenever he has to  undergo any sort of medical procedure in  the season 8 episode the septum  deviation sheldon's worries transfer  over to leonard after a routine checkup  leonard learns he has a deviated septum  that prevents him from breathing  properly he decides to get a small  surgery to correct his condition but  sheldon is appalled believing that it  could lead to all sorts of complications  all through the episode sheldon remains  extremely panicky over his friend's  surgery things come to a head when the  light goes out in the middle of the  operation causing sheldon to run  screaming into the room to try to save  leonard and subsequently crash into a  glass door breaking his nose  to the rest of the world sheldon cooper  might seem like a humorless man who  takes himself way too seriously but his  closest friends know that sheldon has an  impish sense of humor and that he's more  than willing to participate in all kinds  of hijinks with the right companions one  of the most entertaining instances of  this occurs in season 5's the good guy  fluctuation while working late in his  office sheldon is beset by a series of  pranks by raj and howard sheldon manages  to see through all of them with his  trademark air of superiority only to end  up completely freaking out when leonard  sneaks up behind him in a scary mask the  incident leaves a deep impression on  sheldon and he plots his revenge against  the others all through the episode  sheldon tries to play pranks on the  others but his lack of social awareness  and the fact that the others know he's  coming make the pranks fail finally  while leonard is alone in their  apartment musing over some devastating  news sheldon pops up screaming from  beneath his spot on their couch dressed  in zombie makeup for an epically  hilarious prank sheldon never tries to  hide the fact that he considers himself  superior to his friends his dream since  childhood was always to win the nobel  prize for physics the big day finally  arrived in the series finale the  stockholm syndrome sheldon and amy win a  joint nobel for their research in super  asymmetry on the stage after receiving  his award sheldon looks over at leonard  and his friends in the audience and  realizes he's no longer the same man who  years before dreamed only of bragging  about his genius before the world  instead sheldon takes the opportunity to  thank his friends for helping him grow  as a person and as a scientist he calls  each one and asks them to stand then in  his most honest moment on the show says  i apologize if i haven't been the friend  you deserve but i want you to know  in my way  i love you all with that speech sheldon  goes from manchild to mature adult and  acknowledges the almost super-human  patients that leonard and the others had  displayed toward him over the years
 

